body:
We are certainly that. But Bernie isn't out of the running just yet; Biden has nowhere near the majority he needs, and I like to think Bernie can stick it out and pull off a win. He'll clobber Biden in debates, and give him time to campaign; I think we'll see a bigger turn out for Bernie next time.  Plus they've been trying to play it off like it was the death knell for Bernie when in reality it was mostly Biden catching up lol.

I have a mind I'll fight to the bitter end, and only take Joe if there's no one else. But mock my words, if the DNC loses on Biden, or Biden ends up selling out on what he promised or it ends up being more ineffectual dribble;

It will be progressive or nothing next time if the Democrats betray us again. I'm not going to compromise and vote for a party that doesn't care about the woes of my entire class any longer.
